Sval: Remove Firefox's in-app messaging and onboarding

ASRouter delivered Firefox's in-app messages: contextual recommendations,
infobars, Spotlight dialogs, feature callouts, toolbar badges, menu
messages and the background task's toasts. about:welcome was Firefox's
onboarding. Sval turned off every message provider and the onboarding,
so both components go, with about:welcome's name, Spotlight's document,
the background "message" task, the upgrade dialog, the messaging Nimbus
features, the UserMessaging policy, their prefs, strings, styles and
tests, the images only the messages showed, and every trigger the rest
of the browser sent ASRouter.

ASRouterTargeting.sys.mjs stays: it is the targeting environment of
Targeting.sys.mjs, which Nimbus and the background update task read.
asrouter's jar keeps the mail mask glyph FirefoxRelay.sys.mjs shows, and
topsites' jar registers the activity-stream package its tippy-top icons
need. The aboutwelcome Nimbus feature stays as the fixture Nimbus's own
tests read. The compulsory restart notice the update policy shows is a
plain notification bar.

